ACE-FLIP TAKE LEAK -- CONFIRMED (2026-09-01). User hypothesis: in
ace-threshold games the winner gins, so melds matter, not deadwood
-- taking a NON-melding ace flip is a tempo-losing deadwood swap.
  Selection (ace_probe.py, 1200 paired deals, seed 76100):
    non-melding subgroup decline-vs-take +3.00 +/- 2.80 (z=2.1).
  CONFIRMATION (2400 fresh paired deals, seed 76900):
    meldonly - default +4.24 +/- 1.80 overall,
    +4.79 +/- 1.92 on non-melding deals (z=4.9). CONFIRMED.
  v7 takes the non-melding ace 97% of the time (ace melds at deal
  only ~12%); mechanism: the teacher prior prices the take by
  deadwood gain and the 16-step truncated rollouts cannot see the
  tempo cost in a 40+step gin race, so the prior survives.
  Side finding: the -5.85 "hero loses ace games" from the 4800-hand
  MC did NOT replicate (+0.31 +/- 2.00 selection, -1.47 +/- 1.40
  confirm at n=2400... note confirm's default arm slightly negative
  but compatible with ~-1; the -5.85 was subgroup noise).
  FIX DEFERRED until the new home OPENING RULE (below) is in: the
  pass mechanic changes the flip decision's EV structure, and the
  opening study will measure the optimal policy directly.
  Records: results/ace_probe_report.log, ace_probe_confirm.log,
  rows in results/ace_probe_rows.json / ace_probe_confirm_rows.json.
