HOME OPENING RULE -- IMPLEMENTED ENGINE-WIDE (2026-09-01, user
rules decision; closes the "dealer's second option" fidelity gap).
Rule: P1 may take the flip; else P2 may take it (out of turn, play
returns to P1); else P1 MUST draw from stock. Passes move no cards
and are public decline evidence on the flip.
  sim.py: _home_opening state machine in step_fast /
    fast_legal_actions (opening node has the familiar [draw,pickup]
    shape; DrawCardAction there = PASS); HomePassMove (move_sheet) /
    HomePassAction (phase marker); Snap/restore carry the state.
  belief.py: opp pass -> decline evidence. particle.py: new
    opp_pass/hero_pass events (decline term, no _pending).
  pf_expert._resolve maps HomePassMove. evaluate.py: my-pass/
    opp-pass events, history_check rules, legacy-transcript pass
    inference (first-move my-draw with flip on pile => implied
    opp-pass), build_state arms _home_opening (1 = hero first
    option, 2 = hero second after opp-pass), action labels
    "take the flip"/"PASS on the flip". viz.py history labels.
  GATES: home_variant.py --test-opening PASS (scripted sequences,
    snapshot/restore, 300 teacher hands w/ all 3 opening kinds,
    searched v7 self-play hand, belief desyncs 0). sim --verify /
    fullrules / adaptive+ladder parity / anchors ALL GREEN
    (standard game untouched). Evaluator smoke: pos_home1 opening
    reads "take the flip (3H)"; synthetic P2-option position
    (opp-pass event) prices take vs PASS correctly.
  NOTE: home match/MC results gated BEFORE this change (v6home,
    home_mc, ace_probe) were measured without the P2 flip option;
    the opening study below re-measures opening EVs under the
    real rule.
