OPENING-THEORY STUDY -- COMPLETE (2026-09-01/02, 6000 deals x 3
forced arms on the NATIVE opening rule, v7 self-play, seed 77300;
results/opening_report.log, rows results/opening_rows.json).
THE THEORY (both seats, all thresholds):
  TAKE IFF IT MELDS. Melding takes: P1 +11.2/+10.2/+9.6 (A-3/4-7/
  8-10), P2 +19.4/+11.7/+11.6. NON-melding takes: every band a tie
  or negative -- A-3 P1 -2.45+/-2.58, P2 -4.03+/-2.55; 8-10 P1
  -1.03, P2 -1.26; and the big junk swaps (gain 7-10) trend WORST:
  P1 -2.35+/-2.60, P2 -3.87+/-2.54. The teacher's take-iff-gain>=1
  rule gets NO support in any non-melding gain band.
  TEMPO IS WORTH NOTHING: P2 taking a non-melding flip to "go
  first" = -1.29 +/- 1.16 over 5068 deals.
  V7'S GAP: takes 72.7% as P1 / would take 54.5% as P2, vs ~15.5%
  of flips melding -- massive over-taking, consistent with the
  CONFIRMED ace leak (+4.79 for meld-only in A-band) and the same
  16-step-truncation mechanism (the tempo cost is beyond the
  rollout horizon; the deadwood gain is immediate).
  NEXT (bot fix candidate, gate per discipline): meld-only opening
  policy at flip-option nodes (prior override), re-gate v7home.
