P2 SPECULATIVE-TAKE CLAUSE -- CONFIRMED + ADOPTED (2026-09-02).
User hypothesis: the second player's flip take is effectively an
EXTRA TURN, so P2 should take with adjacency >= 2 even non-melding.
  p2adj_gate.py, 3000 paired cell-deals (P1 forced pass, P2
  take-vs-pass on identical deals, seed 79100, sharded):
  dEV(P2 take) +3.05 +/- 1.50 (z=4.0, CI excludes 0);
  by flip band: A-3 +9.11 +/- 3.48 | 4-7 +1.77 +/- 2.54 |
  8-10 +1.42 +/- 2.18 (strongest exactly where games are longest,
  as the extra-turn logic predicts); adj==2 +2.91, adj>=3 +3.96.
  Caveat noted: cell sampled with P1 FORCED to pass (includes ~15%
  P1-melding deals that book-P1 would take in real play).
  BOOK IS NOW: P1 takes iff melds; P2 takes iff melds OR adj >= 2
  (sim.flip_book_take, single source; FastTeacher / HomeV6Policy /
  evaluator / PF option-aware likelihoods 1 vs 2 all follow).
  Gates: --test-opening PASS (both seats book-exact; P2-take
  41->96/300), verify 100.0000%, parity x2, anchors -- ALL GREEN.
  Seat asymmetry now fully measured: the same non-melding adj>=2
  take in A-3 games is -5.47 for P1 and +9.11 for P2.
