OPENING SOLVER -- BUILT, VALIDATED, GATED: NOT ADOPTED (2026-09-02).
User directive: calculate the opening per-hand instead of the book.
  opening_solver.py: full-length paired playouts (K=160, take vs
  pass in identical sampled worlds, teacher/MixedKnock continuation)
  with the book as z=1.5 prior. ~0.6 CPU-s per opening node.
  VALIDATION (300 deals vs the 6000-deal ground truth): every cell
  matches in sign and ordering, mild attenuation at the extremes
  (P2 melding +8.8 vs +13.4; adj0 A-3 -5.9 vs -11.3) -- the
  teacher-playout model compresses effects (results/
  solver_validate.log).
  GATE (2000 paired deals, seed 80900, results/solver_gate.log):
  paired solver - book = -0.53 +/- 0.62 -- the per-hand calculator
  is slightly WORSE than the book. Mechanism: the book IS a
  calculation -- the pooled 6000-deal ground-truth estimator; a
  K=160 per-hand solve with an attenuated playout model adds
  variance (and model error) on top of cells the pooled data
  already measured tightly, and its z=1.5 deviations select noise
  (lesson #3's shape, mild form). The available headroom is tiny:
  the book is provably within ~0.3 pts/hand of optimal opening
  play. NOT ADOPTED; solver kept (HomeV6Policy(solver=True),
  --validate/--gate harnesses) for future retries with a truer
  continuation model or K>=400 + z>=2.5.
  BOOK STANDS: P1 iff melds; P2 iff melds or adj>=2.
