T2 EXCEPTION -- USER CELL REAL, RULE NOT ADOPTED (2026-09-03).
User counterexample: best-case non-melding t2 take (adj-2 ace +
dead-K shed, 10-game). CONSTRUCTED-STATE MEASUREMENT (scenario_
probe.py, 8000 + 6000x14 paired worlds): the cell is genuinely
POSITIVE (+1.12 +/- 0.62 / +1.16 +/- 0.51 base; factor map: needs
adj>=2 AND a dead-10 shed jointly -- threshold and card rank do NOT
matter; adj<=1 or small dump kill it). The pooled slices had hidden
this corner. BUT the operationalized rule (sim.t2_book_take
exception: adj>=2 + best-drop value >= 10) GATED AT A TIE in
natural play: -0.19 +/- 0.87 over 2000 paired deals; fired on 20%
of hands; per-fired-game -0.94 +/- 4.32 (results/t2x_gate.log).
Transfer failure understood: (a) natural triggers are SELECTED --
an opponent discarding your adjacency card is informative in ways
the uniform constructed worlds are not; (b) the operational rule
fires ~40x more often than the pure corner, diluting it. t2x stays
default False; machinery kept (HomeV8Policy(t2x=True),
scenario_probe --map, t2x_gate). The t2 book remains take-iff-
melds. Lesson: constructed-cell EV does not equal natural-play EV
-- gate every rule in situ.

NATURALLY-CONDITIONED T2 STUDY -- USER METHODOLOGY VINDICATES THE
LOW-CARD EXCEPTION; ADOPTED (2026-09-03, nat2_study.py,
results/nat2_study.log, rows nat2_rows.jsonl).
User's methodological correction: rejection-sample fresh deals and
keep only states where the OPPONENT CHOSE to discard the low card
on v8's own line (two-tier: teacher-line screen ~5ms + v8 verify;
natural frequency ~1 in 15,000 hands). 430 accepted paired states:
  ALL (opp-discarded card <=3, adj>=2, non-melding):
    dEV(take) +3.58 +/- 2.41 -- POSITIVE, CI excludes 0.
  scenario 1 (t>=8 & dead-10 shed): +2.87 +/- 3.07
  scenario 2 (t<=3 & top<=2): n=34, unresolved alone
  OUTS strata (user hand-strength measure): weak hands (outs 0-2)
    gain most, +10.96 +/- 7.81 -- the user's "weak hand upgrades
    all future draws" argument CONFIRMED at the low end; middle
    +2-3; strong cell noisy.
RECONCILIATION: the earlier t2x rule tied because it fired on ANY
card value (20% of hands, mostly mid/high where take ~ 0); the
value is specific to LOW cards (<=3). ADOPTED: t2_book_take
exception = value<=3 AND adj>=2 (t2x default True; evaluator
updated). No match gate possible or needed at 1/15000 frequency --
adopted on the causal evidence; it is the theory, at zero cost.
Gates: unit checks, --test-opening, verify -- green.
